Let's face it. Wizards are wimps. And the junky equipment they get stuck
with doesn't help much. So why not stop giving them junky equipment?

The idea is simple: don't give wizards useful or harmful items. And don't
give them two identical rings. ("an uncursed ring of aggravate monster" --
I got two of them once.) Don't give them scrolls of fire, or scrolls of
destroy armor, or potions of blindness. (This last sentence may be disputed
by some who say that knowing those items from the start helps a wizard
avoid them later in the game. But the dispute is moot if the wizard doesn't
make it to later in the game.)

Do you *really* think that J. Random Wizard is going to walk into a dangerous
dungeon, prepared to face unknown perils, equipped with a ring of hunger? Nay,
I say, J. Random is likely to bring along items he'll actually be able to use.
our nethack characters should do no less.

